## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP with dual objectives: minimize cost and count optimal deletion sets, plus implement in two styles. It also covers edge cases like empty substrings and ties.

## Key Concepts
- DP on substrings; store (cost, ways).
- Memoization and bottom-up parallels; careful counting on ties.
- Modulo arithmetic for counts.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Memoized DFS
function solveMemo(s, delCost){
  const n = s.length;
  const memoCost = Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(n).fill(-1));
  const memoWays = Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(n).fill(0));
  const MOD = 1_000_000_007;
  function dfs(l,r){
    if (l>=r) return {cost:0, ways:1};
    if (memoCost[l][r]!==-1) return {cost:memoCost[l][r], ways:memoWays[l][r]};
    if (s[l]===s[r]){
      const res = dfs(l+1,r-1);
      memoCost[l][r]=res.cost;
      memoWays[l][r]=res.ways;
      return res;
    } else {
      const A = dfs(l+1,r);
      const B = dfs(l,r-1);
      let cost;
      let ways = 0;
      if (A.cost + delCost[l] < B.cost + delCost[r]){
        cost = A.cost + delCost[l];
        ways = A.ways;
      } else if (B.cost + delCost[r] < A.cost + delCost[l]){
        cost = B.cost + delCost[r];
        ways = B.ways;
      } else {
        cost = A.cost + Math.min(delCost[l], delCost[r]);
        ways = (A.ways + B.ways) % MOD;
      }
      memoCost[l][r]=cost; memoWays[l][r]=ways;
      return {cost, ways};
    }
  }
  return dfs(0,n-1);
}
```

## Purpose
This problem tests sliding-window aggregation with per-key state management, lazy expiration strategies, and top-K extraction using a heap. It integrates multiple data structures: hashtables for O(1) key lookups, per-key queues for temporal ordering, and a heap for maintaining ranked sums.

## Key Concepts
- **Sliding window maintenance**: Events expire once they exceed the window width W
- **Per-key accumulation**: Each key maintains its own queue of (timestamp, value) pairs
- **Lazy eviction**: Stale entries are removed only when encountered, avoiding unnecessary cleanup
- **Amortized efficiency**: The cost of expiration is distributed across active operations

## Code Example
```javascript
class WindowedTopKMap {
  constructor(windowWidth) {
    this.W = windowWidth;
    this.map = new Map();
    this.heap = new MinHeap();
  }

  addEvent(key, value, ts) {
    if (!this.map.has(key)) {
      this.map.set(key, { sum: 0, queue: [] });
    }
    const entry = this.map.get(key);
    entry.queue.push({ ts, value });
    entry.sum += value;
    this.heap.push({ sum: entry.sum, key });
  }

  advanceTime(now) {
    // Lazy cleanup handled in topKKeys
  }

  topKKeys(K, now) {
    const results = [];
    while (results.length < K && !this.heap.isEmpty()) {
      const top = this.heap.pop();
      const entry = this.map.get(top.key);
      if (!entry) continue;
      this._expire(entry.queue, now);
      if (Math.abs(entry.sum - top.sum) > 0.0001) continue;
      results.push(top.key);
    }
    return results;
  }

  _expire(queue, now) {
    while (queue.length && queue[0].ts <= now - this.W) {
      entry.sum -= queue.shift().value;
    }
  }
}
```

